WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:06.182
Welcome to vNAAATS. In this video you will learn how the flight data display works with natTrak.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:13.158
pending and cleared lists requesting a clearance for an aircraft and answering clearance requests that arrive by CPDLC.

00:00:15.078 --> 00:00:20.838
Please note this is a demonstration using sample flights. It is not a live version of the FDD.

00:00:24.294 --> 00:00:27.654
Sign in to the FDD with your key and it opens on your position.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.806
To work in natTrak itself, press open natTrak and sign in there with your VATSIM details.

00:00:33.062 --> 00:00:35.622
The FDD never sees your natTrak password.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:44.006
At the top, natTrak Pending lists the requests waiting for controller and cleared lists the clearances already issued with the track fixed level, Mach and estimate.

00:00:44.422 --> 00:00:46.566
New requests flash and sound an alert.

00:00:46.854 --> 00:00:50.246
You can switch the visual alert, the sound, the circle, and the tone here.

00:00:53.542 --> 00:00:59.686
Select an aircraft and its natTrak clearance data appears on the right. The status level, Mach fix an estimate.

00:00:59.942 --> 00:01:01.734
You can compare it with the flight plan.

00:01:02.758 --> 00:01:08.422
The pilot has not yet asked for clearance. Auto RCL reminds them for you from 90 to 30 minutes before their entry point.

00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:14.182
If they are on Hoppie it goes as a telex, otherwise it is typed to them in EuroScope and a red star shows it has been sent

00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:18.982
You can also send it yourself. Open the aircraft menu, choose RCL, REQ and press send.

00:01:19.302 --> 00:01:23.174
Inside 30 minutes, it is too late for a request, so deal with that flight on voice.

00:01:23.814 --> 00:01:30.886
Pilots who ask by CPDLC show in the clearance request list at the top of the CPDLC window. Press Prepare and natTrak.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.798
In the Windows app, natTrak opens with the form filled in.

00:01:34.118 --> 00:01:41.254
In a browser, you get the values with a copy button for each. Check them, then press create yourself in natTrak. The FDD never presses it for you.

00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:45.734
Once the flight is on natTrak and you have checked it there, the Send button is unlocked.

00:01:46.214 --> 00:01:53.894
RCL process tells the pilot to fly the current flight plan or is amended by a TC and to squawk 2000 at the oceanic entry point.

00:01:54.374 --> 00:01:56.294
The pilot answers Roger or Wilko.

00:01:56.646 --> 00:01:58.662
Send re-clearance sends the full clearance.

00:01:59.302 --> 00:02:03.142
A preview opens first, check the text, change it if you need to, and press send.

00:02:03.526 --> 00:02:12.006
The message goes from your CPDLC station with the clearance, the squawk instruction and a contact line for Gander, Shanwick or NAT FSS depending on your position.

00:02:12.486 --> 00:02:13.798
The pilot answers will co.

00:02:14.502 --> 00:02:16.710
The request then shows who sent it and when.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.846
You can send it again at any time from the same buttons.

00:02:20.454 --> 00:02:23.750
Always check the clearance in natTrak before you press either button.

00:02:24.454 --> 00:02:26.694
FDD only ever sends what you confirm.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:32.422
You can also pop the CPDLC window out onto a second screen, so request stay in view.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.976
That is natTrak through the FDD. Thanks for watching.

